# DB object index (index.bin)

Verified on the three copies in the game paks and on the mod's `G:\__H5__\heroes-expansion\game_data\core\index.bin` (October 2026), and in Ghidra on H5X.exe. Tool: `tools/h5index/h5index.py` (end of this file).

## What it is

A list of **every DB object of the game data, grouped by class type**: for each `TypeID`, the hrefs of all XDB objects of that type. The engine asks it for "all objects of type X".

**The map editor's object palette is the `AdvMapObjectLink` list**: every indexed link shows up as a placeable object, whatever it points to. The mod's links were picked by hand (commits "add artifact links in index.bin", "creatures links for editor", "editor heroes": 207 links). `game_data/artifacts/MapObjects/_(AdvMapObjectLink)/Artifacts/` also holds 10 link files that must stay out of the index: `Artificier`, `BloodCrystal`, `Freida`, `Graal` (a second Tear of Asha), `PotionOfExperience`, `PotionOfMana`, `PotionOfStamina`, `Princess_Aelina`, `ShantiriEast`, `XXX`. Adding them (2026-10-18) put Shantiri East, Blood Crystal, the potions and a duplicate Tear of Asha in the editor. The palette shows a link under its file name, whether or not its target exists; a link's target does not need to be indexed (most mod artifact map objects were not, and their links showed).

**Editor categories** are defined in `H5Xdev/editor/MapFilters.xml`: each filter lists folder prefixes of `AdvMapObjectLink` files (`MapObjects\_(AdvMapObjectLink)\GenericHeroes\` = ". Heroes (Generic)", `…\Heroes\` = ". Heroes (Scenario)", `…\Monsters\`, `…\Artifacts\`, `…\Towns\`, …). A link with `<Link href>` places that object, a link with `<RndGroup href>` places a random member of an `AdvMapSharedGroup`. `<IconFile>` is relative to `H5Xdev/Complete/` (mod source: `heroes-expansion/editor/Complete/`, deployed by `sync-editor.ps1`). `<HideInEditor>true` hides a listed link: the mod hides vanilla links by overriding the file at the same path. The mod's copy of `MapFilters.xml` is `heroes-expansion/editor/editor/MapFilters.xml` (deployed to `H5Xdev/editor/` by `sync-editor.ps1`); it renames ". Heroes (Generic)" to ". Heroes by class" and ". Heroes (Scenario)" to ". All heroes".

**Icon cache**: the editor renders each link's icon once and keeps it in `H5Xdev/editor/IconCache/AdvMapObjectLink/<link path without .xdb>` (binary saver format). A link whose `IconFile` changes keeps its old icon until that cache file is deleted; new paths are cached on first display. **Delete single entries or folders, never the whole cache**: the vanilla icons are not rebuilt the same way (deleting it on 2026-10-18 removed the icons of every object). `H5Xprod/editor/IconCache` holds a full copy (1,692 entries); the 2026-10-18 restore copied it back, except the links whose `IconFile` exists in `heroes-expansion/editor/Complete` (mod heroes, artifacts and creatures), which are rebuilt from the repo icons.

**Hero palette** (2026-10-18, `heroes-expansion/tools/generators/editor-heroes.py`; after a run, delete the `GenericHeroes` and `Heroes` folders of the icon cache): "Heroes by class" holds the 16 H5X classes. Links are `GenericHeroes/<Class>.xdb` (named after the English class name, reusing the vanilla files `Knight`, `Ranger`, `Runemage`, `Wizard`, `Warlock`, `Barbarian`, `Demonlord`), with `RndGroup` = `/MapObjects/_(AdvMapSharedGroup)/Heroes/Classes/<Class>.xdb` (6 heroes each) and the class icons of `Icons/Generated/…/Classes/`. "All heroes" holds one link per hero of `_(AdvMapSharedGroup)/Heroes/Any.xdb` (96), `Heroes/<Faction>/<English name>.(AdvMapObjectLink).xdb`, with a 128×128 icon made from the hero's `FaceTexture`. Battle Commander heroes (Tazar, Darkstorm) and the Vampire Princess (Tamika) join the might class of their faction. Every other link of both folders is overridden with `HideInEditor` true: vanilla `Necromancer`, `EntryPoint`, the campaign heroes, and the older mod links (`Heaven/`, `ReadHeaven/`, `Neutral/`, …).

**Artifact palette** (`heroes-expansion/tools/generators/editor-artifacts.py`, helpers shared with `editor-heroes.py` in `editor_links.py`): one link `Artifacts/<Name>.(AdvMapObjectLink).xdb` per entry of `Artifacts.xdb` that has an `ArtifactShared` other than the `XXX` placeholder, is not in the `INVENTORY` slot (except the grail, kept in the vanilla `Graal.xdb` path) and is not a `POTION_*`. `<Name>` is the text folder (`/Text/Game/Artifacts/<Name>/`), the icon (64×64) comes from the entry's `Icon`. The `Random-*.xdb` links stay as they are; every other link of the folder is hidden. On 2026-10-18 it gives the 192 artifacts already in the editor plus Dawn Gleam (added 2026-09-19 without a link).

Links with a missing target (2026-10-18): `PhoenixFeather` (→ `PhoenixFeather.(AdvMapArtifactShared).xdb`, removed from the index: it showed a Phoenix Feather that should not be placeable) and `ShacklesOfTheLastMan` (→ `ShantiriNorth.(AdvMapArtifactShared).xdb`, still indexed). `Kujins_Bull` and `Gudkov` are vanilla links with missing targets. The Phoenix Feather Cape texts now belong to `ARTIFACT_DWARVEN_SMITHY_HUMMER` (`PhoenixFeatherCape.(AdvMapArtifactShared).xdb`, link `PhoenixFeatherCape`), and `PHOENIX_FEATHER_CAPE` holds the Solar Ring.

