## Binary layout

Same encoding as the save files (`h5x-re-save-format.mdc`): `tag (1 byte)` + varint length + content, the varint being one byte `n << 1` when `n < 0x80`, else the u32 `(n << 1) | 1`. A file is one saved object:

```
[4] u32 4                                  version
[1] { [2] u32 root_id }                    root object id (any value; 0x1025FED0 in ToE, 0x07DD6EA0 in the mod)
[0] 9 bytes: u32 0x3027D440, u32 root_id, u8 1     object table: one record [type][id][live]
[2] {                                      object chunks
  [1] {
    [0] u32 root_id
    [1] {                                  the index object
      [2] {                                hash_map<u32 TypeID, vector<CDBPtr>>
        [3] u32 count (244)   [4] u32 buckets (389)
        [1] u32 TypeID        × count      keys, in bucket order: key % 389 from high to low
        [2] {                 × count      values, same order
          [2] u32 n
          [1] { [2] href }    × n          CDBPtr saved as its href (latin-1 string)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
[5] empty
```

`h5index.py` rewrites the three copies byte for byte from their parsed content.

## Keys: TypeID

The key is the class `TypeID` of `types.xml` (`game_data/core/types.xml`, also in `data.pak` / `a2p1-data.pak`): `Base/SharedClasses/Item` with `Type` = `TYPE_TYPE_CLASS` gives `TypeName` and `TypeID` (286 classes in the mod's file). `TypeID` is written as a **signed** decimal: the 31 IDs ≥ `0x80000000` (`Camera` `0xB4513180`, `CreatureVisual`, `SpellVisual`, `ArenaBuilding`, `RMGSimpleCustomArmyTemplate`, …) appear negative. The ToE `types.xml` lacks some of the classes its index uses; their IDs can be read back from the index (all hrefs of one key end with the same type name).

Examples: `AdvMapStatic` `0x160BD480` (205,030 hrefs), `AdvMapObjectLink` `0x161312C0`, `AdvMapStaticShared` `0x16130CC0`, `AdvMapMonsterShared`, `AdvMapArtifactShared`, `AdvMapHeroShared`, `Texture` `0x12069B8E`, `WindowSimple` `0x1107C380`. A DB type id is not the runtime class id of the save files (`CWindowSimple` is `0x110772C1` there).

## Which objects are listed

Checked by scanning every `.xdb` of `data.pak` + `a2p1-data.pak` and comparing with the ToE index (all hrefs match except the unshipped files above and 123 shipped objects missing from the index, mostly `UI/CommonBoxes` windows and campaign map objects):

- the **root element** of every XDB file: `/<path>#xpointer(/<Root>)`, e.g. `/MapObjects/Gold_Mine.(AdvMapMineShared).xdb#xpointer(/AdvMapMineShared)`;
- every **inline object with an id**: an element carrying `id="…"` whose first child is a class (`<Item href="#n:inline(AdvMapStatic)" id="item_X"><AdvMapStatic>`): `/<path>#xpointer(id(item_X)/AdvMapStatic)`. Maps, dialog scenes, arenas and effects contribute most of the 312k hrefs this way.

Only class types are listed (structs, enums and tables are not). An object is listed once, under its own type only (not its base classes). `<path>` is the path inside the pak (= inside a `heroes-expansion/game_data/<pak>/` folder), with a leading `/`. Lookups in `h5index.py` ignore case.

## In the exe

| Address | Role |
|---|---|
| `0x00BA0690` | Returns `"index.bin"` |
| `0x00499F90` | Single index ctor (`this`, VFS, load flag), vtable `0x00E1430C`, 0x10 bytes. If the flag is set, reads `index.bin` from that VFS and loads the object (`FUN_0049AE10`); if nothing was loaded, creates an empty map object (`FUN_0049B370`, 0x24 bytes) at `+0xC` |
| `0x004998C0` | Writes `index.bin` (saver vtable `+0xC` with the map object) |
| `0x00499B80` | Re-reads `index.bin` (vtable slot 10) |
| `0x00499850` / `0x00499860` | Vtable `+0x1C` / `+0x20`: forward to the map object at `+0xC` (add object / query a type) |
| `0x0049A0F0` | Composite index ctor, vtable `0x00E14344`: one single index per child VFS |
| `0x0049A210` | Factory: 1 VFS → single index, several → composite |
| `0x00C6CD40` | DB setup: if the data VFS (`+0x70`) is a `NVFS::CCombinerVFS`, takes its children, builds the index (`+0x78`) |
| `0x00499C60` | Composite `+0x20` (query a type): asks each child **from the last to the first** and merges the results, dropping hrefs already returned. Writes (`+0x1C`, `+0x28`) go to the last child |

So every file system combined into the data VFS can carry its own `index.bin`, and the results are merged. The mod ships a full copy (ToE + its additions) in `h5x-core.pak`; duplicates with the ToE copy are dropped at query time. A pak holding only the mod's objects (`--delta`) should work the same if each pak is its own child VFS, but that is **not tested in game**: keep shipping the full copy.

## Mod update of 2026-10-18

`h5index.py update` added 35,795 mod objects to `game_data/core/index.bin` (now 348,279 hrefs, 35.9 MB, deployed in `h5x-core.pak`): 33,133 encyclopedia windows (`UI/Doc`, `www*` paks: `WindowTextView`, `WindowMSButton`, `WindowSimple`, `UISSendUIMessage`, …), then `Creature` 890, `Texture` 555, `Model` 211, `AdvMapArtifactShared` 193, `Material` 172, `BasicSkelAnim` 151, `Character` 46, `Effect` 35, `AdvMapHeroShared` 30, `CreatureVisual` 28, `TownBuildingSharedStats` 22, `AdvMapMonsterShared` 13, `Spell` 3, … The 10 unlisted `AdvMapObjectLink` files were added, then removed again, and the committed `PhoenixFeather` link was removed (see above). The hero palette then added 98 links and the 16 class groups (348,392 hrefs).

## Tool

```bash
python tools/h5index/h5index.py stats   G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data/core/index.bin
python tools/h5index/h5index.py list    G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data/core/index.bin AdvMapObjectLink
python tools/h5index/h5index.py missing G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data/core/index.bin G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data
python tools/h5index/h5index.py update  G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data/core/index.bin G:/__H5__/heroes-expansion/game_data
python tools/h5index/h5index.py diff    old.bin new.bin
MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 python tools/h5index/h5index.py remove <index.bin> "/MapObjects/…#xpointer(/AdvMapObjectLink)" …
```

- `update` keeps every existing entry in place and appends the missing hrefs per type (sorted), then overwrites the index unless `--out` is given. It **skips `AdvMapObjectLink`** (lists them as "not added"): `--links-under PREFIX` (repeatable) adds the missing links of one folder, e.g. `--links-under "/MapObjects/_(AdvMapObjectLink)/Heroes/"` after `editor-heroes.py`; `--links` adds all of them, only when every listed link is wanted.
- `remove` drops the given hrefs (case-insensitive). From Git Bash, set `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`, otherwise arguments starting with `/` are turned into Windows paths and match nothing. `--base toe` rebuilds from the ToE copy of `a2p1-data.pak` instead (drops entries added by hand). `--delta` writes the mod's objects only.
- Type names: `types.xml` next to the index, else `<game_data>/core/types.xml`, completed from the index. Tags without a class TypeID are reported and skipped.
- A full scan of `game_data` (37k XDB files) and a 32 MB load take a few minutes. Then `sync-core.ps1` packs `h5x-core.pak`.
